Changes a method's signature, keeping the half not given.

A patch cannot do this: a receiver and a parameter list in one change each need
their own elision, and two "..." in a signature cross-connect. Only --params is
given here, so the result list survives. The doc comment stays attached, and
"context" is added because the new parameter refers to it.

Call sites are not updated, which is why the caller below still passes nothing.

-- args --
edit method Queue.Wait --params "ctx context.Context" --import context

-- go.mod --
module example.com/typededit

go 1.22

-- app/app.in.go --
package app

// Queue holds work.
type Queue struct {
	Depth int
}

// Wait blocks until the queue drains.
func (q *Queue) Wait() error {
	return nil
}

-- app/app.out.go --
package app

import "context"

// Queue holds work.
type Queue struct {
	Depth int
}

// Wait blocks until the queue drains.
func (q *Queue) Wait(ctx context.Context) error {
	return nil
}
